---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ProductSubNav from '../../../components/ProductSubNav.astro';

const SUBNAV = [
  { label: 'Overview', href: '/products/cordel-connect' },
  { label: 'Compatibility & Matching', href: '/products/cordel-connect/compatibility-and-matching' },
  { label: 'Privacy Architecture', href: '/products/cordel-connect/privacy-architecture' },
  { label: 'Safety', href: '/products/cordel-connect/safety' },
  { label: 'Cartoonized Profiles', href: '/products/cordel-connect/cartoonized-profiles' },
  { label: 'AIya & Aion', href: '/products/cordel-connect/aiya-and-aion' },
  { label: 'Games & Activities', href: '/products/cordel-connect/games-and-shared-activities' },
  { label: 'ByteOracle Horoscopes', href: '/products/cordel-connect/byteoracle-horoscopes' },
  { label: 'Date Planning', href: '/products/cordel-connect/date-planning' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Safety | Cordel Connect | ByteLite LLC"
  description="Cordel Connect's safety toolkit, feature by feature: what's tested and working today, what's private-test only, and what's still in development."
  keywords="Cordel Connect safety, date safety, emergency contacts"
>
  <Header slot="header" />
  <section class="section-sm"><div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Cordel Connect', href: '/products/cordel-connect' }, { label: 'Safety' }]} /></div></section>
  <ProductSubNav items={SUBNAV} />

  <section class="sf-hero">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:820px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Safety</p>
      <h1>Safety treated as a core feature, not an afterthought.</h1>
      <p class="sf-p">
        Meeting a stranger in person is the risky part of online dating, so Cordel Connect is
        building a real safety toolkit around it. Below is each capability's actual current
        status — we'd rather tell you a feature isn't ready than have you rely on one that isn't.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:820px;">
      <div class="sf-list">
        <div class="sf-item">
          <div class="sf-item-head"><h3>Emergency contacts</h3><span class="badge badge-active">Implemented &amp; tested</span></div>
          <p>Add, edit, and store trusted contacts inside the app. This flow is verified end-to-end, including a fix confirmed on real devices.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-item">
          <div class="sf-item-head"><h3>Check-in pins</h3><span class="badge badge-private">Private-test build</span></div>
          <p>Drop a real GPS pin on a map for "I'm leaving," "I've arrived," and "I'm back safe." The code path is wired end-to-end, but we don't yet have on-device proof of the full three-pin flow running start to finish — treat it as private-test quality, not field-proven.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-item">
          <div class="sf-item-head"><h3>Contacting someone, honestly</h3><span class="badge badge-private">Private-test build</span></div>
          <p>When an alert goes out, the app reports which contacts were actually reached versus not, based on real delivery confirmation rather than an assumed "sent" message. A full end-to-end alert-triggering test is still outstanding.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-item">
          <div class="sf-item-head"><h3>Live location sharing</h3><span class="badge badge-planned">In development</span></div>
          <p>Your location is captured and stored when you start a safety session, but it is not yet delivered anywhere a trusted contact can actually see it. <strong>Don't rely on this to let someone track you in real time yet</strong> — that connection isn't built.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-item">
          <div class="sf-item-head"><h3>Spoken safety phrase</h3><span class="badge badge-planned">In development</span></div>
          <p>You can set and save a safety phrase today. Saying it out loud does not yet do anything — voice detection isn't connected to safety alerts yet. <strong>Treat this as inactive until we say otherwise.</strong></p>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-item">
          <div class="sf-item-head"><h3>Never impersonates police/911, never secretly records</h3><span class="badge badge-active">True by design</span></div>
          <p>There is no recording capability anywhere in the app, and calling 911 places a real phone call — it never simulates one.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sf-limits">
        <h3>Limitations that apply across all of this</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Every safety feature needs an active internet connection — nothing works offline.</li>
          <li>Location is only read while the app is open in the foreground; there is no background tracking yet.</li>
          <li>Contact delivery is best-effort SMS. It is not guaranteed, and the app tells you honestly when a message fails rather than claiming it succeeded.</li>
          <li><strong>Cordel is not a replacement for emergency services.</strong> If you are in danger, call 911 or your local emergency number yourself.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="asset-ph-grid" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;max-width:340px;margin:0 auto;">
        <img src="/cordel/screenshots/15_safety_hub.png" alt="Cordel Connect safety hub screen" style="width:100%;border-radius:1.25rem;border:1px solid #1a2235;" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>

<style>
.sf-hero { padding: 4.5rem 0 3.5rem; }
.sf-p { font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #a0a8c0; }
.sf-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem; }
.sf-item { padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .75rem; }
.sf-item-head { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: .5rem; }
.sf-item-head h3 { margin: 0; color: #e4e7f2; font-size: 1.0625rem; }
.sf-item p { margin: 0; color: #a0a8c0; font-size: .9375rem; line-height: 1.7; }
.sf-item p strong { color: #f472b6; }
.sf-limits { margin-top: 2rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid #1a2235; }
.sf-limits h3 { color: #e4e7f2; font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: .75rem; }
.sf-limits ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; color: #7b829e; font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.8; }
</style>
